| ADR index | `docs/adr-support.md` |
| Option mappings | `docs/res/config.md` |
| Agent index | `AGENTS.md` |

Conflict resolution: `docs/sdd.md` > `docs/implementation.md`.

## Module map

| Package | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `domain/` | Frozen types: IDs, modes, options, project, catalog, execution, reports |
| `config/` | Project config discovery, schema, loader |
| `catalog/` | Bundled catalog YAML, validation, loader |
| `planning/` | Workflows, suites, scopes, request resolution |
| `adapter/` | Resolved request → argv serialization |
| `runtime/` | Executor, install, environment, reports, cache, parallel, remote |
| `normalize/` | Tool output → canonical `CheckReport` |
| `formatters/` | Canonical report → human/CI text |
| `gates/` | Project-local script gates |
| `frontend/` | Report HTTP API and UI |
| `plugins/` | Plugin catalog and normalizer loading |
| `app.py` | Orchestration with dependency injection |
| `cli.py` | argparse entrypoint only |
| `api.py` | Public Python API |

## ADR invariants

- ADR-001: Policy separate from execution
- ADR-002: Execution Request is the internal API
- ADR-003: Tools and suites are runnables
- ADR-004: Normalize before format
- ADR-005: Plugin API via entry points
- ADR-006: Opinionated defaults
- ADR-007: Familiar UX, metadata-driven internals
- ADR-008: Seed catalog from prior tool set
- ADR-009: SonarQube-inspired frontend on canonical reports
